that maps a repository to an SPDX identifier (for example, GitHub's license
detection) will therefore report this repository as "no license detected" or
`NOASSERTION`. That is an artifact of SPDX recognition, not an absence of a
license: the CSL 1.0 text in `LICENSE-SPEC` is the governing license.

Source code and scripts in this repository (for example, under `scripts/` and
`conformance/`) are provided under the same CSL 1.0 terms. The reference
implementation is a separate repository, licensed under Apache-2.0.
